data.content:
In .NET 10 (starting with .NET 9 SR10+), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated on Android because the underlying `adjustResize` mode was removed by Android itself (API 30+).

The recommended replacement is to use **edge-to-edge rendering** with `KeyboardInsets`. Here's how:

**1. Enable edge-to-edge in your `MainActivity`:**

```csharp
protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);
    AndroidX.Core.View.WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);
}
```

**2. Use `android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustNothing"` in `AndroidManifest.xml`:**

```xml
<activity android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustNothing" ... />
```

**3. Listen for keyboard insets and adjust your layout with a `Behavior` or padding:**

In your page or a custom handler, apply bottom padding based on the IME inset:

```csharp
#if ANDROID
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
    Platform.CurrentActivity!.Window!.DecorView, 
    new InsetsListener(yourBottomBar));

class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    readonly View _target;
    public InsetsListener(View target) => _target = target;

    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        _target.TranslationY = -imeInsets.Bottom / 
            DeviceDisplay.MainDisplayInfo.Density;
        return insets;
    }
}
#endif
```

**Alternatively**, the simplest cross-platform approach in .NET 10 is to wrap your content in a `ScrollView` or use the community `KeyboardBehavior` from the MAUI Community Toolkit, which handles this for you on both platforms:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns:toolkit="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2022/maui/toolkit">
    <Grid>
        <Grid.Behaviors>
            <toolkit:KeyboardBehavior />
        </Grid.Behaviors>
        <!-- your chat list + input bar -->
    </Grid>
</ContentPage>
```

**TL;DR:** Replace the deprecated `adjustResize` with AndroidX Window Insets listeners (edge-to-edge) or use the MAUI Community Toolkit's `KeyboardBehavior` for a drop-in solution.
